#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:7
msgid "Automation rules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:9
msgid "Automation rules allow the execution of one or more predefined actions in response to a specific trigger, e.g., create an activity when a field is set to a specific value, or archive a record 7 days after its last update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:13
msgid "When creating an automation rule, :ref:`domain filters <general/automation-rules/conditions>` allow you to add conditions that must be met for the automation rule to run, e.g., the opportunity must be assigned to a specific salesperson, or the state of the record must not be :guilabel:`Draft`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:18
msgid "Automation rules are provided by the *Automation Rules* module (`base_automation`). If the menu described below is not available, go to the :guilabel:`Apps` app, remove the :guilabel:`Apps` filter from the search bar, search for `Automation Rules`, and click :guilabel:`Activate`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:23
msgid "Managing automation rules requires :ref:`developer mode <developer-mode>` and the *Administration / Settings* access rights."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:26
msgid "To create an automation rule, proceed as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:28
#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules/webhooks.rst:54
msgid "With :ref:`developer mode activated <developer-mode>`, go to :menuselection:`Settings --> Technical --> Automation --> Automation Rules`, then click :guilabel:`New`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:30
msgid "Select the :guilabel:`Model` the automation rule applies to, e.g., :guilabel:`Sales Order`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:31
msgid "Give the automation rule a clear, meaningful name that identifies its purpose."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:32
msgid "Select the :ref:`trigger <general/automation-rules/trigger>` and, if necessary, fill in the fields that appear on the screen based on the chosen trigger."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:34
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Add an action`, then select the :guilabel:`Type` of :ref:`action <general/automation-rules/action>` and fill in the fields that appear on the screen based on your selected action."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:37
msgid "Save the automation rule."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:50
msgid "To ensure follow-up on less satisfied clients, this automation rule creates an activity 3 months after a sales order is created for clients with a satisfaction percentage lower than 30%."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:64
msgid "Use the :guilabel:`Notes` tab to document the purpose and functioning of automation rules. This makes rules easier to maintain and facilitates collaboration between users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:66
msgid "The model targeted by the automation rule is set in the :guilabel:`Model` field of the automation rule form."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:68
msgid "Automation rules can be created from any kanban stage by clicking the :icon:`fa-cog` :guilabel:`(Settings)` icon that appears when hovering over the kanban stage name, then selecting :guilabel:`Automations`. In this case, the :guilabel:`Trigger` is set to :guilabel:`Stage is set to` by default, but it can be changed if necessary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:85
msgid "Trigger"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:87
msgid "The :guilabel:`Trigger` is used to define what kind of event needs to occur for the automation rule to run. The available triggers depend on the model. Five trigger categories are available overall:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:91
msgid ":ref:`general/automation-rules/trigger-values-updated`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:92
msgid ":ref:`general/automation-rules/trigger-email-events`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:93
msgid ":ref:`general/automation-rules/trigger-timing-conditions`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:94
msgid ":ref:`general/automation-rules/trigger-custom`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:95
msgid ":ref:`general/automation-rules/trigger-external`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:100
msgid "Adding conditions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:102
msgid "Domain filters allow you to determine the records an automation rule should target or exclude. Efficient filtering enhances overall performance as it avoids unnecessary processing on records that are not impacted by the rule."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:107
msgid ":ref:`Activate developer mode <developer-mode>` before creating an automation rule to have the most flexibility in adding domain filters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:110
msgid "Depending on the trigger chosen, it is possible to define one or more conditions a record must meet *before* and/or *after* a trigger occurs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:113
msgid "The :guilabel:`Before Update Domain` defines the conditions a record must meet *before* the trigger event occurs, e.g., the record must have `Type = Customer Invoice` and `Status = Posted`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:116
msgid "With :ref:`developer mode activated <developer-mode>`, click :guilabel:`Edit Domain`, if available, then :guilabel:`New Rule`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:119
msgid ":guilabel:`Extra Conditions`, or in some cases :guilabel:`Apply on` filters, define the conditions a record must meet *after* the trigger event occurs, e.g., the customer invoice must have `Payment Status = Partially Paid`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:123
msgid "With :ref:`developer mode activated <developer-mode>` if needed, click :guilabel:`Add conditions` or :guilabel:`Edit Domain`, as relevant, then :guilabel:`New Rule`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:126
msgid "When a :ref:`trigger <general/automation-rules/trigger>` occurs, e.g., the payment status of a posted customer invoice is updated, the automation rule checks the defined conditions and only executes the :ref:`action <general/automation-rules/action>` if the record matches those conditions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:131
msgid "If the automated action should be executed when an email address is set for the first time (in contrast to modifying an email address) on an existing contact that is an individual rather than a company, use `Email is not set` and `Is a Company is not set` as the :guilabel:`Before Update Domain` and `Email is set` as the :guilabel:`Apply on` domain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:146
msgid "The :guilabel:`Before Update Domain` is not checked upon the creation of a record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:151
msgid "Values Updated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:153
msgid "Trigger automated actions when specific changes happen in the database. The triggers available in this category depend on the model and are based on common changes, such as adding a specific tag (e.g., to a task) or setting a field's value (e.g., setting the :guilabel:`User` field)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:157
msgid "Select the trigger, then select a value if required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:162
msgid "Email Events"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:164
msgid "Trigger automated actions upon receiving or sending emails:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:166
msgid ":guilabel:`On incoming message`: when a message is received on the record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:167
msgid ":guilabel:`On outgoing message`: when a message is sent from the record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:169
msgid "These triggers are only available for models that have a chatter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:174
msgid "Timing Conditions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:176
msgid "Trigger automated actions at a point in time relative to a date field or to the creation or update of a record. The following triggers are available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:179
msgid ":guilabel:`Based on date field`: The action is triggered a defined period of time before or after the date of the selected date field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:181
msgid ":guilabel:`After creation`: The action is triggered a defined period of time after a record is created and saved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:183
msgid ":guilabel:`After last update`: The action is triggered a defined period of time after an existing record is edited and saved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:186
msgid "You can then define:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:188
msgid "a :guilabel:`Delay`: Specify the number of minutes, hours, days, or months. To have an action executed before the trigger date, specify a negative number. If you selected the :guilabel:`Based on date field` trigger, you must also select the date field to be used to determine the delay."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:193
msgid "By default, the scheduler checks for time-triggered automation rules every 240 minutes, or 4 hours. This frequency is generally sufficient for delays such as 3 months after the order date or 7 days after the last update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:197
msgid "For delays of less than the equivalent of 2400 minutes, or 40 hours, the system recalculates the frequency of this check to ensure that more granular delays, e.g., 1 hour before the event start date and time, or 30 minutes after creation, can be respected as closely as possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:201
msgid "An on-screen message indicates the possible delay after the scheduled triggering of the rule."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:211
msgid "To view or manually edit the frequency of the scheduler, with :ref:`developer mode activated <developer-mode>`, go to :menuselection:`Settings --> Technical --> Scheduled Actions` to see all scheduled actions for your database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:215
msgid "Enter `Automation` in the search bar, then, in the list of results, click :guilabel:`Automation Rules: check and execute`. If desired, update the value of the :guilabel:`Execute Every` field. Click :guilabel:`Run Manually` at any time to manually trigger this scheduled action."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:219
msgid ":guilabel:`Extra Conditions`: Click :guilabel:`Add condition`, then specify the conditions to be met for the automation rule to run. Click :guilabel:`New Rule` to add another condition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:222
msgid "The action is executed when the delay is reached and the conditions are met."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:225
msgid "To send a reminder email 30 minutes *before* the start of a calendar event, select :guilabel:`Start (Calendar Event)` as the date field for the :guilabel:`Trigger` and set the :guilabel:`Delay` to `-30` :guilabel:`Minutes`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:241
msgid "Custom"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:243
msgid "Trigger automated actions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:245
msgid ":guilabel:`On save`: when a record is saved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:246
msgid ":guilabel:`On deletion`: when a record is deleted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:247
msgid ":guilabel:`On archived` / :guilabel:`On unarchived`: when a record is archived or restored, for models that can be archived."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:249
msgid ":guilabel:`On UI change`: when a field's value is changed on the Form view, even before the record is saved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:252
msgid "For the :guilabel:`On save` and :guilabel:`On UI change` triggers, you **must** then select the field(s) to be used to trigger the automation rule in the :guilabel:`When updating` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:256
msgid "If no field is selected in the :guilabel:`When updating` field, the automated action may be executed multiple times per record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:259
msgid "Optionally, you can also define additional conditions to be met to trigger the automation rule in the :guilabel:`Apply on` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:263
msgid "To trigger an automated action *upon* the creation of a record, e.g., when a new contact is created, select the :ref:`On save <general/automation-rules/trigger-custom>` trigger and use `ID is not set` as the :guilabel:`Before Update Domain` and `ID is set` as the :guilabel:`Apply on` domain. Make sure the correct field is selected in the :guilabel:`When updating` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/automation_rules.rst:269
msgid "When a new contact is saved, it is automatically assigned a database ID, thereby triggering the automation rule."
msgstr ""

