#: ../../content/applications/general/users/2fa.rst:42
msgid "Two-factor authentication setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/2fa.rst:44
msgid "After selecting an authenticator, log in to Odoo, then click the profile avatar in the upper-right corner, and select :guilabel:`My Profile` from the resulting drop-down menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/2fa.rst:47
msgid "Click the :guilabel:`Account Security` tab, then slide the :guilabel:`Two-Factor Authentication` toggle to *active*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/2fa.rst:57
msgid "This generates a :guilabel:`Security Control` pop-up window that requires password confirmation to continue. Enter the appropriate password, then click :guilabel:`Confirm Password`. Next, a :guilabel:`Two-Factor Authentication Activation` pop-up window appears, with a |QR|."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/2fa.rst:69
msgid "Using the desired authenticator application, scan the |QR| when prompted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/2fa.rst:72
msgid "If scanning the screen is not possible (e.g. the setup is being completed on the *same* device as the authenticator application), clicking the provided :guilabel:`Cannot scan it?` link, or copying the secret to manually set up the authenticator, is an alternative."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/2fa.rst:89
msgid "Afterwards, the authenticator should display a *verification code*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/2fa.rst:97
msgid "Enter the code into the :guilabel:`Verification Code` field, then click :guilabel:`Activate`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/2fa.rst:107
msgid "Logging in"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/2fa.rst:109
msgid "To confirm |2fa| setup is complete, log out of Odoo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/2fa.rst:111
msgid "On the login page, input the username and password, then click :guilabel:`Log in`. On the :guilabel:`Two-factor Authentication` page, input the code provided by the chosen authenticator in the :guilabel:`Authentication Code` field, then click :guilabel:`Log in`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/2fa.rst:123
msgid "If a user loses access to their authenticator, an administrator **must** deactivate |2fa| on the account before the user can log in. To do so, open the user's form in :menuselection:`Settings --> Users & Companies --> Users`, go to the :guilabel:`Account Security` tab, and switch off the :guilabel:`Two-factor Authentication` toggle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/2fa.rst:129
msgid "Trusted devices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/2fa.rst:131
msgid "On the |2fa| login page, tick :guilabel:`Don't ask again on this device` to skip the code on that browser for a while. The devices trusted this way are listed in the :guilabel:`Trusted Devices` section of the :guilabel:`Account Security` tab of the user's preferences. Click the :icon:`fa-trash` :guilabel:`(delete)` icon next to a device to revoke it, or :guilabel:`Revoke All` to revoke all of them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/2fa.rst:138
msgid "Enforce two-factor authentication"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/2fa.rst:140
msgid "To enforce the use of |2fa| for all users, first navigate to :menuselection:`Main Odoo Dashboard --> Apps`. Remove the :guilabel:`Apps` filter from the :guilabel:`Search...` bar, then search for `2FA by mail`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/2fa.rst:144
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Install` on the Kanban card for the :guilabel:`2FA by mail` module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/2fa.rst:153
msgid "After installation is complete, go to :guilabel:`Settings app: Permissions`. Tick the checkbox labeled, :guilabel:`Enforce two-factor authentication`. Then, use the radio buttons to choose whether to apply this setting to :guilabel:`Employees only`, or :guilabel:`All users`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/2fa.rst:158
msgid "Selecting :guilabel:`All users` applies the setting to portal users, in addition to employees."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/2fa.rst:167
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Save` to commit any unsaved changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/2fa.rst:169
msgid "Users who have not configured an authenticator app then receive a verification code by email when logging in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:3
msgid "Access management"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:5
msgid "The *Access Management* module (`eyssen_access_management`) gives administrators three additional tools to control what a user can reach, on top of the standard :doc:`access rights <access_rights>`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:9
msgid ":ref:`IP subnets <access-management/ip-subnets>` from which a user is allowed, or not allowed, to log in;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:11
msgid ":ref:`restricted menus <access-management/menus>`, to hide menu items from a user;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:12
msgid ":ref:`model domain rules <access-management/domain-rules>`, to reserve a set of records for some users in the views."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:15
msgid "It also keeps a :ref:`log of the logins <access-management/logins>` of every user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:18
msgid "To install the module, go to :menuselection:`Settings --> eYssen ERP`, and, in the :guilabel:`General Modules` section, enable :guilabel:`Access Management`. See :doc:`../eyssen_erp_settings`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:21
msgid "All the features described on this page are only available to users whose :guilabel:`Administration` access right is set to :guilabel:`Access Rights` or :guilabel:`Settings`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:25
msgid "The rules can be managed from two places:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:27
msgid "on the user: go to :menuselection:`Settings --> Users & Companies --> Users`, open a user, and click the :guilabel:`Access Management` tab, which contains the :guilabel:`IP Subnets`, :guilabel:`Restricted Menus`, and :guilabel:`Model Domain Rules` sub-tabs;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:30
msgid "for all users at once: from the :menuselection:`Settings --> Access Management` menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:43
msgid "IP subnets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:45
msgid "An IP subnet rule restricts the network addresses from which a user can log in through the login page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:48
msgid "To create a rule, go to :menuselection:`Settings --> Access Management --> IP Subnets`, click :guilabel:`New`, and fill in the following fields:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:51
msgid ":guilabel:`Rule`: :guilabel:`Allow` or :guilabel:`Deny`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:52
msgid ":guilabel:`Type`: :guilabel:`IPv4` or :guilabel:`IPv6`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:53
msgid ":guilabel:`IP Subnet`: the subnet in CIDR notation, e.g., `192.0.2.0/24`. To target a single address, enter the address alone (`192.0.2.78`) or with a `/32` suffix. An invalid subnet is refused when the rule is saved;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:56
msgid ":guilabel:`Users`: the users the rule applies to;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:57
msgid ":guilabel:`Company`: optionally, the company the rule belongs to;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:58
msgid ":guilabel:`Description`: a free text, e.g., the name of the office."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:60
msgid "The same rule can be assigned to several users. In the lists, :guilabel:`Allow` rules are displayed in green and :guilabel:`Deny` rules in red."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:63
msgid "When a user logs in, the rules assigned to them are evaluated as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:65
msgid "If the user has no rule, they can log in from anywhere."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:66
msgid "If the user has at least one :guilabel:`Allow` rule, they can only log in from an address that belongs to one of the allowed subnets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:68
msgid "If the user only has :guilabel:`Deny` rules, they can log in from anywhere, except from the denied subnets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:70
msgid "A :guilabel:`Deny` rule always wins: use it to exclude a smaller subnet, or a single address, from an allowed subnet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:73
msgid "A user who tries to log in from a forbidden address gets the message *Access from this IP address is not allowed*, and the attempt is recorded in the :ref:`login log <access-management/logins>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:77
msgid "Overlapping subnets are not checked. Review the rules of a user as a whole before saving, in particular for your own administrator account, to avoid locking yourself out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:79
msgid "The address taken into account is the one transmitted by the reverse proxy in front of the database. If all logins appear to come from the same internal address, ask your system administrator to check the proxy configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:86
msgid "Restricted menus"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:88
msgid "Menu items can be hidden user by user, without creating a dedicated user group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:90
msgid "Open the :guilabel:`Restricted Menus` sub-tab of the user's :guilabel:`Access Management` tab and choose how the list works with the :guilabel:`Hide all menu items` toggle:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:93
msgid "**disabled** (default): all the menu items the user has access to are displayed, *except* the ones added to the list;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:95
msgid "**enabled**: all menu items are hidden, *except* the ones added to the list (and provided the user has access to them)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:98
msgid "Then, click :guilabel:`Add a line` and select the menu items. Both applications (top-level menus) and sub-menus can be selected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:102
msgid "When :guilabel:`Hide all menu items` is enabled, remember to add the parent menus as well: a sub-menu whose application is hidden cannot be reached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:105
msgid "The reverse view is available on the menu items: in :ref:`developer mode <developer-mode>`, go to :menuselection:`Settings --> Technical --> User Interface --> Menu Items`, open a menu item, and click the :guilabel:`Restricted Users` tab. A user displayed in red sees everything but this menu item; a user displayed in green sees nothing but the menu items explicitly allowed, including this one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:112
msgid "Menu restrictions are ignored for users whose :guilabel:`Administration` access right is :guilabel:`Access Rights` or :guilabel:`Settings`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:114
msgid "Hiding a menu item only removes it from the navigation. It does not change the user's access rights on the underlying records; use :doc:`groups and access rights <access_rights>` for that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:117
msgid "The user has to reload the page for a change to be taken into account."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:130
msgid "Model domain rules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:132
msgid "A model domain rule reserves a set of records for one or more users: the records matching the rule are only listed for the users of the rule, and are left out of the views of everybody else."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:135
msgid "To create a rule, activate the :ref:`developer mode <developer-mode>` (the filter editor is only displayed in developer mode), go to :menuselection:`Settings --> Access Management --> Model Domain Rules`, click :guilabel:`New`, and fill in:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:139
msgid "the name of the rule;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:140
msgid ":guilabel:`Users`: the users for whom the records are reserved;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:141
msgid ":guilabel:`Company`: optionally, the company in which the rule applies. A rule without a company applies in every company;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:143
msgid ":guilabel:`Lines`: click :guilabel:`Add a line`, select a :guilabel:`Model` (e.g., *Sales Order*), and define the :guilabel:`Filter Domain` with the domain editor. A rule can contain lines for several models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:147
msgid "Finally, the rule can also be assigned from the :guilabel:`Model Domain Rules` sub-tab of a user's :guilabel:`Access Management` tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:150
msgid "For each model, the records displayed to a user are determined as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:152
msgid "records that do not match any rule line with users remain visible to everybody;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:153
msgid "records that match a rule line are only visible to the users of that rule;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:154
msgid "records that match a line of a rule **without** any user are visible to everybody, even if another rule reserves them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:158
msgid "The rule *Key accounts* has the users *Anita* and *Marc*, and one line on the model *Sales Order* with the filter `Customer > Tags contains \"Key account\"`. The quotations and sales orders of the key accounts are now only listed for Anita and Marc; all the other orders remain visible to the whole sales team."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:164
msgid "Model domain rules filter the records loaded in the views of the web client (list, Kanban, etc.). They are not a security mechanism: totals of grouped views, pivot and graph analyses, exports, and printed reports are not filtered, and a record can still be opened with a direct link. For a strict restriction, ask your system administrator to set up record rules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:169
msgid "The rules never apply to the *Users*, *Contacts*, and *Companies* models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:180
msgid "IP subnets, model domain rules and their lines cannot be deleted from the interface. To stop using an IP subnet rule, remove its users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:186
msgid "Restrict journals to users"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:188
msgid "With the *Access Management - Account* module (`eyssen_access_management_account`), a journal can be reserved for some users without writing a domain by hand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:191
msgid "Go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Journals`, open a journal, click the :guilabel:`Advanced Settings` tab, and select the users in the :guilabel:`Limited Users` field of the :guilabel:`Access Rules` section. The field is not available on journals of the :guilabel:`Miscellaneous` type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:196
msgid "Each time a journal is saved, the rules of the :guilabel:`Automatic` type are rebuilt: one rule named *Access Management Rule for Journals* is created per group of users, with lines on the journals, the journal entries (and therefore the invoices and bills), and the journal items. As a result, the limited journals and their entries are only listed for the selected users. Automatic rules are read-only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:202
msgid "In addition, the :menuselection:`Accounting --> Reporting --> Management --> Invoice Analysis` report only includes the invoices of the journals that are either not limited, or limited to the current user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:206
msgid "To install the module, enable :guilabel:`Account` under :guilabel:`Access Management` in :menuselection:`Settings --> eYssen ERP`. In the same place, the :guilabel:`PoS` option installs the restriction of points of sale by user; see the :ref:`point of sale configuration <pos/configuration/access-rules>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:222
msgid "User logins"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:224
msgid "Every login attempt made on the login page with an existing user name is recorded with the :guilabel:`User`, the :guilabel:`IP Address`, the browser (:guilabel:`User Agent`), and, for a failed attempt, the :guilabel:`Reason`: *Wrong login/password* or *Access from this IP address is not allowed*. Successful logins are displayed in green and failed attempts in red."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:229
msgid "To see the logins of one user, open the user and click the :guilabel:`Logins` smart button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:230
msgid "To see all logins, go to :menuselection:`Settings --> Access Management --> User Logins`. Use the :guilabel:`Success` and :guilabel:`Unsuccess` filters, the :guilabel:`Date` filter, and group the list by :guilabel:`User`, :guilabel:`IP Address`, :guilabel:`Reason`, or :guilabel:`Date`, e.g., to spot repeated failed attempts from one address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:235
msgid "The log is read-only. Attempts made with a user name that does not exist are not recorded in this list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:247
msgid ":doc:`access_rights`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_management.rst:248
msgid ":doc:`2fa`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:5
msgid "*Access rights* are permissions that determine the content and applications users can access and edit. In Odoo, these permissions can be set for individual users or for groups of users. Limiting permissions to only those who need them ensures that users do not modify or delete anything they should not have access to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:10
msgid "**Only** an *administrator* can change access rights."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:13
msgid "Making changes to access rights can have a detrimental impact on the database. This includes *impotent admin*, which means that no user in the database can make changes to the access rights. For this reason, Odoo recommends contacting an Odoo Business Analyst, or our Support Team, before making changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:19
msgid "A user **must** have the specific *Administration* access rights set on their user profile, in order to make changes on another user's settings for access rights."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:22
msgid "To access this setting, navigate to :menuselection:`Settings app --> Manage users --> select a user --> Access Rights tab --> Administration section --> Administration field`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:25
msgid "Once at the setting, an already existing administrator **must** change the setting in the :guilabel:`Administration` field to :guilabel:`Access Rights`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:28
msgid "Once complete, click :guilabel:`Save` to save the changes, and implement the user as an administrator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:36
msgid "The access rights for :ref:`individual users <users/add-individual>` are set when the user is added to the database, but they can be adjusted at any point in the user's profile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:39
msgid "To make changes to a user's rights, click on the desired user to edit their profile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:48
msgid "On the user's profile page, in the :guilabel:`Access Rights` tab, scroll down to view the current permissions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:51
msgid "For each app, use the drop-down menu to select what level of permission this user should have. The options vary for each section, yet the most common are: :guilabel:`Blank/None`, :guilabel:`User: Own Documents`, :guilabel:`User: All Documents`, or :guilabel:`Administrator`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:55
msgid "The :guilabel:`Administration` field in the :guilabel:`Access Rights` tab has the following options: :guilabel:`Settings` or :guilabel:`Access Rights`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:69
msgid "Create and modify groups"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:71
msgid "*Groups* are app-specific sets of permissions that are used to manage common access rights for a large amount of users. Administrators can modify the existing groups in Odoo, or create new ones to define rules for models within an application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:75
msgid "To access groups, first activate Odoo's :ref:`developer mode <developer-mode>`, then go to :menuselection:`Settings app --> Users & Companies --> Groups`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:85
msgid "To create a new group from the :guilabel:`Groups` page, click :guilabel:`Create`. Then, from the blank group form, select an :guilabel:`Application`, and complete the group form (detailed below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:88
msgid "To modify existing groups, click on an existing group from the list displayed on the :guilabel:`Groups` page, and edit the contents of the form."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:91
msgid "Enter a :guilabel:`Name` for the group and tick the checkbox next to :guilabel:`Share Group`, if this group was created to set access rights for sharing data with some users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:95
msgid "Always test the settings being changed to ensure they are being applied to the correct users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:97
msgid "The group form contains multiple tabs for managing all elements of the group. In each tab, click :guilabel:`Add a line` to add a new row for users or rules, and click the :icon:`fa-times` :guilabel:`(cancel)` icon to remove a row."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:109
msgid ":guilabel:`Users` tab: lists the current users in the group. Users listed in black have administrative rights. Users without administrative access appear in blue. Click :guilabel:`Add a line` to add users to this group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:112
msgid ":guilabel:`Inherited` tab: Inherited means that users added to this group are automatically added to the groups listed on this tab. Click :guilabel:`Add a line` to add inherited groups."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:116
msgid "For example, if the group *Sales/Administrator* lists the group *Website/Restricted Editor* in its :guilabel:`Inherited` tab, then any users added to the *Sales/Administrator* group automatically receive access to the *Website/Restricted Editor* group, as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:120
msgid ":guilabel:`Menus` tab: defines which models the group can have access to. Click :guilabel:`Add a line` to add a specific menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:122
msgid ":guilabel:`Views` tab: lists which views in Odoo the group has access to. Click :guilabel:`Add a line` to add a view to the group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:124
msgid ":guilabel:`Access Rights` tab: lists the first level of rights (models) that this group has. The :guilabel:`Name` column represents the name for the current group's access to the model selected in the :guilabel:`Model` column."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:128
msgid "To link a new access right to a group, click :guilabel:`Add a line`. Select the appropriate model from the :guilabel:`Model` drop-down, then enter a name for the access right in the :guilabel:`Name` column. For each model, enable the following options as appropriate:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:132
msgid ":guilabel:`Read`: Users can see the object's existing values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:133
msgid ":guilabel:`Write`: Users can edit the object's existing values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:134
msgid ":guilabel:`Create`: Users can create new values for the object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:135
msgid ":guilabel:`Delete`: Users can delete values for the object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:138
msgid "While there are no conventions for naming access rights, it is advisable to choose a name that identifies its purpose."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:141
msgid "For example, the access that purchase managers have to the :guilabel:`Contact` model could be named `res.partner.purchase.manager`. This consists of the technical name of the model, followed by a name identifying the group of users in question."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:152
msgid "To find the model's technical name from the current view, first enter a placeholder text in the :guilabel:`Name` field, then click the :guilabel:`Model` name, then the :icon:`fa-arrow-right` :guilabel:`(Internal link)` icon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:156
msgid ":guilabel:`Record Rules`: lists the second layer of editing and visibility rights. :guilabel:`Record Rules` overwrite, or refine, the group's access rights. Click :guilabel:`Add a line` to add a record rule to this group. For each rule, choose values for the following options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:160
msgid ":guilabel:`Apply for Read`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:161
msgid ":guilabel:`Apply for Write`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:162
msgid ":guilabel:`Apply for Create`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:163
msgid ":guilabel:`Apply for Delete`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:166
msgid "Record rules are written using a *domain*, or conditions that filter data. A domain expression is a list of such conditions. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:169
msgid "`[('mrp_production_ids', 'in', user.partner_id.commercial_partner_id.production_ids.ids)]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:171
msgid "This record rule is to enable MRP consumption warnings for subcontractors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:173
msgid "Odoo has a library of preconfigured record rules for ease of use. Users without knowledge of domains (and domain expressions) should consult an Odoo Business Analyst, or the Odoo Support Team, before making changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:180
msgid "Superuser mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:182
msgid "*Superuser mode* allows the user to bypass record rules and access rights. To activate *Superuser mode*, first, activate :ref:`developer mode <developer-mode>`. Then, navigate to the *debug* menu, represented by a :icon:`fa-bug` :guilabel:`(debug)` icon, located in the top banner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:186
msgid "Finally, towards the bottom of the menu, click :guilabel:`Become Superuser`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:189
msgid "Only users with *Settings* access for the *Administration* section of the *Access Rights* (in their user profile) are allowed to log in to *Superuser mode*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/users/access_rights.rst:193
msgid "*Superuser mode* allows for circumvention of record rules and access rights, and therefore, should be exercised with extreme caution."
msgstr ""

