#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:3
msgid "Value scheduler"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:5
msgid "The *eYssen Value Scheduler* application (`value_scheduler`) changes the value of one field on many records at once, from a two-column CSV or Excel file, either immediately or at a date and time chosen in advance. Typical examples are price list tags that must be switched at the start of a promotion, or product attributes to be updated for a whole supplier catalog during the night."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:10
msgid "Every operation relies on a **preset**, prepared once by an administrator, which defines the model and the field to update and how the records are found. The users then only have to upload a file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:14
msgid "The application requires the *Price List Validation by Tags* module (`eyssen_product_pricelist_tag`), which is installed along with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:22
msgid "In the :doc:`access rights <users/access_rights>` of a user, the :guilabel:`Value Scheduler` category has two levels:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:25
msgid ":guilabel:`Scheduler`: can open the application, and create, process, schedule, and cancel imports with the existing presets;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:27
msgid ":guilabel:`Administrator`: in addition, has access to the :guilabel:`Developer` menu: the :guilabel:`Preset Editor` and the list of :guilabel:`All Scheduled Changes`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:33
msgid "Import a file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:35
msgid "Open the :guilabel:`Value Scheduler` app, and, in the :guilabel:`Operations` menu, click the operation to perform (e.g., :guilabel:`Pricelist Tag Update`). The list of the previous imports of that operation is displayed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:38
msgid "Click :guilabel:`New`, and upload the file in the :guilabel:`File` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:39
msgid "Select the :guilabel:`Run Mode`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:41
msgid ":guilabel:`Timed`: the changes are applied at the :guilabel:`Scheduled Date`, which becomes mandatory;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:43
msgid ":guilabel:`Instant`: the changes are applied as soon as the file is processed. This mode is limited to 25 changes per import."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:46
msgid "Select the :guilabel:`Write Mode`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:48
msgid ":guilabel:`Overwrite`: the value of the file replaces the current value of the field. For a tags field, an empty second column empties the field;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:50
msgid ":guilabel:`Extend`: for a tags field, the values of the file are added to the existing ones;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:51
msgid ":guilabel:`Remove`: for a tags field, the values of the file are removed from the existing ones. Tick :guilabel:`Clear All` to empty the field instead, whatever the second column contains. For any other field, the field is emptied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:55
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Process`. The file is read, one *scheduled change* is created per row, and the file is attached to the chatter of the import. If a row cannot be interpreted (e.g., an unknown tag name), the whole file is refused, and the message lists the rows to correct."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:59
msgid "In :guilabel:`Timed` mode, the import and its changes move to the :guilabel:`Scheduled` status. In :guilabel:`Instant` mode, the changes are executed right away, and the import moves to :guilabel:`Done`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:72
msgid "File format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:74
msgid "The file is either a CSV file (`;` separator, UTF-8 or Latin-1 encoding) or an Excel workbook (`.xlsx`), of which only the first sheet is read. The first row is a header and is ignored. Each following row has two columns:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:78
msgid "the **lookup value**, used to find the record(s) to update. The field it is compared with is defined by the preset (e.g., the internal reference of the product). Rows with an empty first column are skipped;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:81
msgid "the **new value**. How it is interpreted depends on the preset; for the *Pricelist Tag Update* preset, it is a comma-separated list of price list tag names (not case-sensitive)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:91
msgid "Do not use apostrophes (`'`) in the lookup values: such rows cannot be matched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:96
msgid "Follow up and cancel an import"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:98
msgid "Scheduled changes are applied by the *Value Scheduler: Process Timed Changes* scheduled action, which runs every five minutes and processes the due changes in batches of 25, until none is left. A change is therefore applied within a few minutes after its :guilabel:`Scheduled Date`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:102
msgid "On the import, the :guilabel:`Changes` smart button and the :guilabel:`Scheduled Changes` tab show the changes with their :guilabel:`Lookup` value, the :guilabel:`Modifier` (the value of the file), and, once executed, the :guilabel:`Old Value` and the :guilabel:`Result`. Click the :icon:`fa-search` icon of a line to open the matching records. The status of a change is one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:108
msgid ":guilabel:`Draft`: created, not queued yet;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:109
msgid ":guilabel:`Scheduled`: waiting for its date;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:110
msgid ":guilabel:`Done`: the value was changed;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:111
msgid ":guilabel:`Unchanged`: the records already had the requested value;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:112
msgid ":guilabel:`Failed`: the change could not be applied; the reason is given in the :guilabel:`Notes` tab of the change (e.g., no record found for the lookup value)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:115
msgid "An import is :guilabel:`Done` when all its changes have been processed without failure, and :guilabel:`Failed` if at least one of them failed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:118
msgid "The following buttons are available on the import:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:120
msgid ":guilabel:`Cancel`: on a :guilabel:`Scheduled` import of which no change has been executed yet, moves the import to :guilabel:`Cancelled`; its changes go back to :guilabel:`Draft` and are not applied;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:123
msgid ":guilabel:`Reset to Draft`: brings the import back to :guilabel:`Draft`, together with its scheduled and failed changes, e.g., to modify the scheduled date;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:125
msgid ":guilabel:`Schedule`: on a draft import that already has changes, queues them again without reading the file a second time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:128
msgid "Only draft imports can be deleted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:131
msgid "In :guilabel:`Instant` mode, a *Value Scheduler* note is posted in the chatter of each updated record, with the old value, the value of the file, and the resulting value. Changes applied by the scheduled action do not post such a note, and the usual field tracking is disabled in both modes: use the :guilabel:`Old Value` and :guilabel:`Result` columns of the import as the audit trail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:140
msgid "Presets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:142
msgid "Presets are managed by the administrators of the application in :menuselection:`Value Scheduler --> Developer --> Preset Editor`. A preset is defined by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:145
msgid ":guilabel:`Name` and :guilabel:`Menu Name`, the label of its entry in the :guilabel:`Operations` menu;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:147
msgid ":guilabel:`Target Model` and :guilabel:`Target Field`: the model and the field to update;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:148
msgid ":guilabel:`Domain Lookup Field`: the technical name of the field of the target model that is compared with the first column of the file;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:150
msgid ":guilabel:`Code`: optionally, Python code that converts the rows of the file into changes, e.g., to turn tag names into records and to report unknown names. Without code, the second column is written as is, which suits text and number fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:154
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Install` to create the entry of the preset in the :guilabel:`Operations` menu, and :guilabel:`Uninstall` to remove it. The :guilabel:`Imports` smart button lists the imports made with the preset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:158
msgid "The application is delivered with one preset, *Pricelist Tag Update*, which updates the :guilabel:`Pricelist Tags` of the products."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:162
msgid "The *Pricelist Tag Update* preset is delivered with `master_article_number` as :guilabel:`Domain Lookup Field`. This field is not part of the standard product form: before installing the preset, replace it with the field that identifies your products in the file, e.g., `default_code` (internal reference) or `barcode`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:166
msgid "The code of a preset is executed on the server. Only trusted administrators should be granted the :guilabel:`Administrator` level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:169
msgid ":menuselection:`Value Scheduler --> Developer --> All Scheduled Changes` lists the changes of all imports, with filters by status and grouping by import, model, and scheduled date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/general/value_scheduler.rst:182
msgid ":doc:`../essentials/export_import_data`"
msgstr ""
